# Systems 2: Simulation

The time response of a linear system is known exactly, so a simulation should not be an approximation. This chapter shows how to run a continuous or discrete model on an input, from any initial state, with a choice of how the input is held between samples.

- [Simulating a system](lti_02_simulation/simulating_a_system.md)

